# PTR_GUARD allowlist -- reviewed non-canonical / intentional `as *u8` sites.
#
# Format: <path><TAB><lineno>   (both absolute-path and repo-relative accepted
# only as an exact match on the path the scanner was given)
#
# A pin is a REVIEW RECORD, not a suppression. Every line below states why the
# site is sound. Adding a pin without that sentence is how a guard dies.
#
# Two categories are pinned:
#   (R) INTENTIONAL REPRODUCERS. Files whose entire purpose is to demonstrate
#       the B17 defect, so they must contain the construct. Pinning these is
#       what lets the guard run over the corpus at all. If any of these files
#       is deleted, its pins must be deleted too.
#   (I) INTEGER RECONSTRUCTION. Pointer addresses stored as two i32 halves in
#       arena cells and rebuilt on the far side of a driver/learner boundary.
#       Fed by _zag_slice_ptr on the store side, so it is the sanctioned
#       mechanism, not a slice cast.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# (I) gen_cogops_unify -- the driver stores each heap slice's address as two
#     i32 cells (8000..8028) via `_zag_slice_ptr(b) as i64`, and the glue
#     rebuilds `lo|(hi<<32)` and casts THAT to *u8. The operand is an integer
#     expression, not a slice, so B17 does not apply. Verified: the store side
#     at gu_glue.zag:62 / gu_full.zag:472 uses _zag_slice_ptr.
docs/lab/research-lead/overnight-20260928/gen_cogops_unify/gu_glue.zag	37
